ict";n.d(t,{},{M:["React","Web Components","Vue","Svelte","Storybook","Javascript","Swift","Swift UIKit","Objective-C UIKit","SwiftUI","Compose","Java","Kotlin","Android XML Layout","Flutter","Markdown"]})},234650(e,t,n){"use strict";n.d(t,{jKT:()=>X,Ifg:()=>q,x8v:()=>Q,nn$:()=>Z,Y9L:()=>W,b1X:()=>K,vkO:()=>$,qaI:()=>H,NEL:()=>x,d1E:()=>w,fLQ:()=>V,Ob1:()=>G,YHz:()=>z,oAo:()=>U,xyD:()=>j,pkL:()=>B,HHR:()=>ee,Zj1:()=>J,lqp:()=>v,sjb:()=>u,A$X:()=>g,jAH:()=>f,pvU:()=>c,$8z:()=>I,uft:()=>p,CaX:()=>h,VLE:()=>T,n7l:()=>m,REo:()=>_,o6r:()=>b,J9x:()=>y,TSV:()=>A,npl:()=>Y});var i=n(115629),r=n(811078);let a=e=>i.bl(e,{target:"draft-7",io:"input"});function s(){return`SKILLS (Prefer the skills shipped with the Figma plugin on the agent being used. If no Figma plugin is installed, use the skills served by the Figma MCP resource):
- /figma-use \u{2014} MANDATORY before calling use_figma; fallback: skill://figma/figma-use/SKILL.md
- /figma-generate-design \u{2014} for translating an app page or layout into Figma; fallback: skill://figma/figma-generate-design/SKILL.md
- /figma-generate-library \u{2014} for building a design system in Figma from code; fallback: skill://figma/figma-generate-library/SKILL.md
- /figma-code-connect \u{2014} for mapping Figma components to codebase components; fallback: skill://figma/figma-code-connect/SKILL.md
- /figma-use-figjam \u{2014} for FigJam-specific use_figma flows; fallback: skill://figma/figma-use-figjam/SKILL.md
- /figma-generate-diagram \u{2014} MANDATORY before calling generate_diagram; fallback: skill://figma/figma-generate-diagram/SKILL.md
- /figma-design-to-code \u{2014} MANDATORY before calling get_design_context; fallback: skill://figma/figma-design-to-code/SKILL.md`}let o=`

FILE SESSION:
Once the target fileKey is known, call create_session with that key and a concise task description before search_design_system, get_libraries, use_figma, or any other file tool. This applies to read-only tasks too. If a new file is needed, call create_new_file first, then create_session with the returned file key. Reuse the returned UUID as the sessionId argument on eligible file tools for subsequent work on that task, including calls to other files.`;function l(e){return`

DESIGN-TO-CODE WORKFLOW (Figma \u{2192} code):
MANDATORY: load the /figma-design-to-code skill BEFORE calling get_design_context \u{2014} it carries the full workflow (adapting the reference, reusing existing project components and tokens, and honoring the response's hints by priority). ${e?"After create_session, call":"Call"} get_design_context with the nodeId and fileKey \u{2014} it is your primary tool; its output is a REFERENCE to adapt to the target project, not final code.`}function d(e,t){return`The official Figma MCP server. Use this server whenever the user wants to create, generate, edit, implement, or sync any design, UI, screen, component, mockup, or visual \u{2014} in Figma, FigJam, Figma Make, or Figma Slides \u{2014} and whenever the user mentions Figma or provides a figma.com URL.

This server bridges code and design in both directions, and supports designing from scratch using existing design systems and codebases.${t?o:""}

CAPABILITIES:
- Read designs FROM Figma into code (get_design_context, get_screenshot, get_metadata, get_figjam)
- Write designs INTO Figma from code, intent, or existing components (use_figma, generate_figma_design, create_new_file, upload_assets)
- Bridge code and design via Code Connect (get_code_connect_map, add_code_connect_map)
- Create diagrams and FigJam content (generate_diagram, get_figjam)

WHEN TO USE THESE TOOLS:
- The user wants to create, mock up, or generate any UI, screen, component, or design \u{2014} even if Figma isn't named
- The user wants to implement a design as code (design-to-code)
- The user wants to push a page, view, or component into Figma (code-to-design)
- The user wants to update, sync, or edit an existing Figma file
- The user shares a figma.com URL
- The user wants to build or extend a design system, design tokens, or component library
- The user wants to create a diagram in FigJam

${e}

URL PARSING:
Extract fileKey and nodeId from Figma URLs:
- figma.com/design/:fileKey/:fileName?node-id=:nodeId \u{2192} convert "-" to ":" in nodeId
- figma.com/design/:fileKey/branch/:branchKey/:fileName \u{2192} use branchKey as fileKey
- figma.com/make/:makeFileKey/:makeFileName \u{2192} use makeFileKey
- figma.com/board/:fileKey/:fileName?node-id=:nodeId \u{2192} FigJam file, use get_figjam
- figma.com/slides/:fileKey/:fileName?node-id=:nodeId \u{2192} Figma Slides file`}d(s(),!1),l(!1),d(s(),!0),l(!0);let c="get_design_context",u="get_code",p="get_image",m="get_screenshot",h="get_metadata",g="get_code_connect_map",f="get_code_connect_suggestions",_="get_strategy_for_mapping",y="send_code_connect_mappings",A="send_get_strategy_response",b="get_variable_defs",I="get_figjam",v="add_code_connect_map",x="set_codegen_config";function E(e){return e?" For Figma Specs (figspec), use this tool for creation and edits. Omit currentPageId; the Specs agent resolves the document. For a new Specs file, say creation is underway and the user can open it to follow along. Use /spec/ for Specs links.":""}a(r.s_2),a(r.qGn),!function(e=!1){E(e)}(),function(e=!1){E(e)}();let S=e=>"Send a prompt to Figma Code to create or edit a code-backed app. "+(void 0===e?"Code agent only; no Design Agent or native shapes. Requires edit access.\n\n":`Requires edit access.

${e}

`)+"Standalone Code files use their main layer. In Design, supply nodeId to edit a code layer; omit nodeId and threadId to create one on pageId (default: first page). Omit threadId to reuse the default conversation in Design or start a fresh one in standalone Code. Reuse the returned threadId for follow-ups, with its nodeId in Design. Legacy layers are unsupported.\n\nTo attach local files, set attachment_count to 1\u201310 with your prompt. Returns one upload slot per file without starting generation. Upload all files (up to 5 MiB each, within one hour), then follow nextStep.thenCall, filling in filenames and MIME types in slot order. Keep its prompt and target fields unchanged. The resumed call attaches the files to the conversation and runs the Code agent. Works on populated targets; does not replace the repository or scaffold the uploads. Omit attachment_count or set 0 for a prompt without uploads. Failed uploads must not be resumed.\n\nFor project initialization and scaffolding, use send_code_to_figma when available; follow up with send_prompt if needed.\n\nAfter generation is accepted, returns fileUrl, nodeId, fileKey, threadId and runId. Wait pollAfterMs, then poll check_prompt_status with fileKey and runId. Send one message per target at a time. Do not automatically retry ambiguous failures.\n\nFor awaitingUserAnswers, mirror one question in the client's native question UI using question, options, multiSelect and askUserQuestionContext verbatim. Call send_prompt with continuation set to its resume fields and the answer as prompt. Omit nodeId, pageId, threadId and attachment fields.";S(),S('Set agent "design" only if the user explicitly asks for the Figma Design agent or continues its conversation. Design only: prompt, fileKey, pageId/threadId; no nodeId/attachments/continuation. Uses AI credits. Poll check_prompt_status with fileKey and threadId. Review fileUrl; await approval to code.'),S('For Design, use agent "design". Open once with open_figma_mcp_app_in_thread if available; reuse it for follow-ups. Reopen only if closed, switching files or asked. Design only: prompt, fileKey, pageId/threadId; no nodeId/attachments/continuation. Uses AI credits. Poll check_prompt_status with fileKey and threadId. Review fileUrl; await approval to code.');let T="get_motion_context",w=`IMPORTANT: After you call this tool, you MUST call ${m} to get a screenshot of the node for context.`,C="If the URL is of the format https://figma.com/design/:fileKey/branch/:branchKey/:fileName then use the branchKey as the fileKey.",k="Use the nodeId parameter to specify a node id. If no node id is provided, the currently selected node will be used. If a URL is provided, extract the node id from the URL, for example, if given the URL https://figma.com/design/:fileKey/:fileName?node-id=1-2, the extracted nodeId would be `1:2`.",R="Get design context for a Figma node \u2014 the primary tool for design-to-code workflows. Returns reference code, a screenshot, and contextual metadata that must be adapted to the target project. \n\nIMPORTANT: You MUST load figma-design-to-code guidance BEFORE calling this tool. Prefer the /figma-design-to-code skill if available; otherwise read the skill://figma/figma-design-to-code/SKILL.md MCP resource. \n\nNEVER call this tool without loading that guidance first \u2014 skipping it produces code that ignores the target project's existing components, design tokens, and conventions.\n\n";function P({isRemote:e,includeMakeInstruction:t,includeScreenshotHint:n,includeQueryHint:i}){let r=i?'\n\nJSON projection mode: pass `format: "json"` with a `query` (a CSS selector, same grammar as `node.query()` in the Plugin API) to skip codegen and return a structured list of matched nodes instead of code \u2014 use it to read specific fields from specific nodes rather than generating a whole screen. The `format`, `query`, `depth`, `values`, and `limit` parameters document the full mechanics.':"";return e?R+"Use the nodeId parameter to specify a node id. Use the fileKey parameter to specify the file key. If a URL is provided, extract the node id and file key from the URL, for example, if given the URL https://figma.com/design/:fileKey/:fileName?node-id=1-2, the extracted nodeId would be `1:2` and the fileKey would be `:fileKey`. If the URL does not include `node-id`, ask the user for a node-specific URL. Do not pass an empty or guessed nodeId. "+C+" "+(t?"If the URL is of the format https://figma.com/make/:makeFileKey/:makeFileName then use the makeFileKey to identify the Figma Make file. ":"")+"Only for Figma Make files (URLs containing `/make/`), and only when calling get_design_context, assume the nodeId is `0:1`. The response will contain a code string and a JSON of download URLs for the assets referenced in the code."+(n?" It will also include a screenshot of the node for context by default.":"")+r:R+k+" "+C+(n?" It will also include a screenshot of the node for context by default.":"")+r}function N({isRemote:e}){return e?"Generate UI code for a given FigJam node in Figma. Use the nodeId parameter to specify a node id. If no node id is provided, use `0:1` which is the root node ID. Use the fileKey parameter to specify the file key. If a URL is provided, extract the node id from the URL, for example, if given the URL https://figma.com/board/:fileKey/:fileName?node-id=1-2, the extracted nodeId would be `1:2` and the fileKey would be `:fileKey`. IMPORTANT: This tool only works for FigJam files (URL path `/board/`), not other Figma files.":"Generate UI code for a given FigJam node or the currently selected FigJam node in the Figma desktop app. Use the nodeId parameter to specify a node id. If no node id is provided, the currently selected node will be used. If a URL is provided, extract the node id from the URL, for example, if given the URL https://figma.com/board/:fileKey/:fileName?node-id=1-2, the extracted nodeId would be `1:2`. IMPORTANT: This tool only works for FigJam files (URL path `/board/`), not other Figma files."}function O(e){let t=e.passThroughSkillInstructions??!1;return"- `instructions`: The user's modification request, close to verbatim"+(t?" \u2014 but treat any explicit values from the user's prompt or an invoked /skill (named fonts, hex codes, named components, specific weights/sizes) as user-authored constraints to thread through, not as embellishment to strip":"")+". The agent makes its own design decisions, so don't add your own design specs or invent details"+(t?" the user didn't ask for":"")+" \u2014 that overrides the agent's judgment and tends to produce generic results. DO resolve short or anaphoric follow-ups by stitching in conversation context the agent doesn't have"+(t?", including skill-specified values that should apply to the edit":"")+'.\n  - Example \u2014 User: "Make a blue button" \u2192 "Make a blue button" (NOT "Create a button with border-radius: 8px, blue background (#0066FF), white text, padding 12px..."'+(t?" \u2014 that's your invention, not the user's spec":"")+')\n  - Example \u2014 User (after asking for 5 buttons): "One less" \u2192 "One less button" (NOT "One less" \u2014 the agent doesn\'t know what "one less" refers to)'+(t?'\n  - Example \u2014 User (with a /skill invoked that names "Helvetica" as the typeface): "Update the header text" \u2192 "Update the header text using Helvetica" (thread the skill\'s named font through \u2014 it counts as user input, not your embellishment)':"")}N({isRemote:!1}),!function({includePlaywrightInstruction:e,includeHtmlToFigmaGuidance:t}){}({includePlaywrightInstruction:!0,includeHtmlToFigmaGuidance:!1});let D="- `designSystem`: Pass through the JSON output from the `explore-design-systems` subagent verbatim \u2014 its `relevantComponents` / `relevantStyles` / `relevantVariables` arrays of `{assetId, name, libraryName, guidelines}` map directly onto this field. Forward all entries in full; the agent decides what to use.";function M(e){return"A design agent that modifies existing Figma layer trees \u2014 refining layouts, restyling, rearranging content, polishing visuals, and restructuring. Applies its own design judgment. Works on layers both within and outside of components.\n\n"+(e.omitParameterDocs?"":"**Parameters:**\n\n- `editableNodeIds` (required): Nodes the agent will modify.\n\n"+O(e)+'\n\n- `references`: Existing designs the agent should read but not modify.\n  - `nodeIds`: Node IDs already in the file \u2014 frames as style/layout reference (e.g. "make this card match the style of this other section"), or raster image nodes the user imported (screenshots, photos, mockups). Pass actual node IDs so the agent reads the layer tree and the rendered visual; the server picks the right treatment per node.\n\n'+D+"\n\n")+"**Limitations:**\n- Cannot find or search for nodes \u2014 provide all node IDs upfront\n- Cannot create components, component sets, styles, or variables (but can use those provided)\n- Cannot create or edit vector paths \u2014 only basic shapes and built-in icons\n- Can generate new images but cannot edit pixels of existing images\n\nFor non-typographic edits (color, fill, layout, spacing, sizing, effects), call with `proceedWithMissingFonts` set to true from the first attempt when local fonts are unavailable \u2014 preserve existing text and typography and mention the limitation only if it affects the result. If the edit is primarily a font, typography, or text-rewrite change and target nodes have missing fonts, explain that local fonts are not supported. Only after the user explicitly accepts proceeding, call again with `proceedWithMissingFonts` set to true."}function F(e){return"Use for creative edits, redesigns, and visual polish. Works inside and outside components. This tool only edits Figma Slides files; Design and FigJam files fail.\n\n**Providing context \u2014 the agent only sees what you pass:**\n- `editableNodeIds`: Nodes the agent will modify. Required for editing existing designs.\n- `references`: Designs to read but not modify (`nodeIds` in the file).\n- `designSystem`: Pass through the `explore-design-systems` result verbatim.\n"+(e.serverThemes?"\nLeave `themes` unset \u2014 the server reads the deck's themes. Name theme tokens in `instructions`.\n":"- `themes`: Slide theme variables and styles.\n")+'\n**`instructions` \u2014 pass intent, not implementation:**\nThe agent makes its own design decisions. Don\'t expand the request with your own design specs, but DO add relevant conversation-history context (the agent has no memory of prior turns).\n- If the user points to speaker notes as the content source, read them first and pass their relevant content and constraints. Preserve labels, approximate dates, relative positions, and other relationships even when shortening the visible copy.\n- Preserve existing slide content unless the user asks to remove it or it must change to complete the edit. Leave the layout choice to the agent when the user leaves it open.\n- After "create 5 buttons" then "One less", pass "One less button" (a bare "One less" lacks the referent).\n\n**Limitations:**\n- Cannot find/search nodes \u2014 provide all node IDs upfront.\n- Cannot create components, component sets, styles, or variables (but can use those provided).\n- Cannot create or edit vector paths \u2014 only basic shapes and built-in icons.\n- Can generate new images but cannot edit existing images.\n\nIf the tool fails because target nodes have missing fonts, explain that local fonts are not supported in the remote edit environment. Only after the user explicitly accepts proceeding despite missing fonts or incorrect typography, call again with proceedWithMissingFonts set to true.'}function L(e){let t=!0===e.fileBrowserReadOnly;return(t?"Read an existing Figma file with JavaScript and the Figma Plugin API.\n\n**This tool is read-only in the file browser.** Use it only to inspect nodes and properties or capture screenshots. Never create, change, rename, move, or delete nodes or other file contents. When the user asks to edit a file, start its in-file agent with `seed_thread_for_file` instead.\n":!0===e.readOnlyLead?"Read the Figma scene graph with the Plugin API.\n\n**This tool reads; it does not design.** Visual changes go to `edit_design`, however small. Write here only for what it cannot do.\n":"Execute JavaScript with Figma Plugin API access. Best for precise, verifiable changes and inspecting node properties.\n")+"\n"+(!0===e.make?"Plugin API reference: https://developers.figma.com/docs/plugins/api/. Consult it when an API signature is unclear.\n":!0===e.conditionalTypingsLookup?"Plugin API typings are available at `${ACTIVE_WORKSPACE}/docs/evaluate_script/figma-plugin-api.d.ts`. Grep them when an API name, signature, property, or enum is unclear, or after a related error. Do not preflight routine calls when the API is already clear from the tool schema and current context.\n":"**Before writing, grep the Plugin API typings (`${ACTIVE_WORKSPACE}/docs/evaluate_script/figma-plugin-api.d.ts`) for the exact `figma.*` signatures, properties, and enums you will use \u2014 a wrong name fails the whole call.**\n")+"Each call runs in a fresh scope \u2014 re-fetch nodes by id; nothing persists between calls.\n\n**Parameters:** name the code argument `code`, never `script` (else validation fails).\n\n**Critical \u2014 these crash or silently fail otherwise:**\n- Top-level `await`/`return` work \u2014 do NOT wrap code in an async IIFE. MUST `await` every async call (unawaited ones fail silently and time out).\n- Look up nodes with `await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id)` (null if stale) \u2014 not the sync `figma.getNodeById`.\n"+(t?"":"- Load fonts before any text edit: `await figma.loadFontAsync(node.fontName)`.\n")+"- Follow the current editor guidance for node traversal and inspection. Do not assume node-specific properties such as `children`, `layoutMode`, fills, or effects exist on every node.\n- JavaScript runtime, no TypeScript syntax. `figma.notify()` is a no-op; `figma.viewport.bounds`/`.zoom` throw \u2014 to place elements in the user's view, use the Viewport bounds from the user message. `currentPage`/selection are yours, not the user's \u2014 switch with `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)`.\n"+(!0===e.make?"- Read and edit an existing Design file using its fileKey from the /design/ URL. Use the target Design file key, not the Make file key. Edits require user edit access.\n":t?"- Reads only the file identified by the fileKey passed, load `read-file-context` first before using.\n":"- Writes target current file only. To read another accessible file, load `read-file-context` first, then pass its fileKey.\n")+"\n**Output:** `return <value>` and `console.log()` are captured; uncaught errors propagate. "+(!0===e.discourageStringify?"Return values should be JSON data types, do not stringify them. Avoid including indentation when stringifying console output. ":"")+"`await node.screenshot()` attaches a PNG inline. For `$fig` plan/query wrappers, it flushes the plan and resolves to the same materialized wrapper; raw `SceneNode.screenshot()` resolves to `undefined`. Large output is truncated.\n\n**Limitations:** no network/`fetch()`; no `figma.showUI()`.\n"}M({}),M({omitParameterDocs:!0}),r.OXL.extend({instructions:r.OXL.shape.instructions.describe(r.OXL.shape.instructions.description+"\n"+O({})),designSystem:r.OXL.shape.designSystem.describe(r.OXL.shape.designSystem.description+"\n"+D),references:r.OXL.shape.references.unwrap().extend({nodeIds:r.OXL.shape.references.unwrap().shape.nodeIds.describe(r.OXL.shape.references.unwrap().shape.nodeIds.description+' Frames provide style/layout context (e.g. "make this card match the style of this other section"). The agent reads their layer trees and properties, without rendered images. Do not pass raster images or screenshots.')}).optional().describe(r.OXL.shape.references.description)}),F({}),F({serverThemes:!0}),L({}),L({make:!0}),L({fileBrowserReadOnly:!0}),